From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:15:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] deployment: pace isolate analysis through elastic
 capacity

Module analysis creates one isolate request per non-dependency module,
evaluates its import graph in V8 without supported asynchronous ops, and can
keep up to ANALYZE_CONCURRENCY attempts active. Rejected-before-execution and
overload responses can also create bounded retries. This work bypasses
application action limits while still consuming shared-base isolate workers,
active-JavaScript permits, CPU, and queue entries.

Make the degradable-query leader semaphore an application-scoped admission
object shared with isolate analysis. Preserve immediate typed deferral for
degradable cache-miss leaders, but make each isolate module attempt wait fairly
for one permit before queue admission and release it before retry backoff. This
keeps degradable leaders plus active analysis attempts within the configured
elastic cap without reserving an idle worker. When the cap is unset, analysis
retains its previous behavior.

A queued analysis waiter receives released capacity before a later immediate
degradable acquisition, providing bounded-class progress whenever existing
permit holders complete. Normal queries, dependencies, mutations, actions,
Node analysis, configuration evaluation, worker eligibility, and dependency
reserve remain unchanged.

Expose analysis reservation occupancy and gate-wait metrics. Add focused
fairness and capacity-transfer tests, and document patch composition, source
evidence, sizing limits, a worked capacity example, rollout, rollback, and a
controlled deployment experiment.
